  "title": "Identify thread creator in '@' list",
  "content": "<p>When you type ‘@’, you get a list of thread contributors.</p><p>It would be useful if that list identifies which one started the thread.</p><p> </p><p>Also, It seems to me that the thread starter (almost?) always appears at the very end of the list - which seems unhelpful.</p><p> </p><p><strong><u>PS</u>:</strong></p><p>Also, the list includes <em>my own username</em> - which seems pointless ?</p><p> </p><p>Example:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/c0df8698-2aa0-48b4-94c9-dd7d8bb548db.png\" /></figure><p> </p>",
